  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies the optimal architecture as multimodal/multiprofile/transformer/weighted with imagenet_vit_l (config_039, acc 0.7250), and scvi_n200 clearly outperforms scgpt (0.72+ vs 0.52). However, pca_n2000 as an RNA encoder has never been tested in the multimodal setting, leaving an important uncertainty: whether a simpler linear representation could match or complement the learned scvi_n200 embedding when fused with the image modality. Config_029 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) isolates this single variable within the best-known architecture. If it underperforms scvi_n200 (likely), it confirms scvi_n200 is the right choice and we can confidently exploit the config_039 neighborhood in the remaining 3 experiments. If it performs comparably or better, it reveals a new direction. With only 3 experiments left, resolving this last major encoder uncertainty is the highest-value use of experiment 7 before committing the final budget to exploitation."
